    "message": "13.32% of protein intensity in the worst file, 1.34% median across 12 files (DEF-QC-9 v3.5)"
   },
   {
    "code": "low_core_use",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "14.56 avg cores of 32 allowed (S5)"
   },
   {
    "code": "occupancy_not_stored",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "Of 18544 occupancy entries MetaMorpheus wrote, some are not in ptm_stoichiometry: 1040 site not in ptm_sites. 'site not in ptm_sites' means the entry's site has no ptm_sites row to key on; 'not determinable' means a cell's segments could not be assigned to its accessions from the sequences (QuantProject DEF-OCC-ACCESSION), which is never guessed. Absence of a row for these sites is therefore not NA. A 'duplicate' is a second entry for a (site, run) that already has a row: one with identical values loses nothing; one with DIFFERENT values means MetaMorpheus wrote two answers and the first in file order was stored (examples in bundle.json occupancy.differing_duplicates; which one should be stored is QuantProject's to define)."
   },
   {
    "code": "peptide_rows_localization_ambiguous",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "67 row(s) of AllQuantifiedPeptides.tsv name several full sequences, joined by `|`: a peptide whose modification site the search did not settle (MetaMorpheus #2917). Their 141 value(s) are not stored, since storing them under one of the sequences would place them on a site the search never decided. The PSMs behind them are in `psms`. E.g. `AADK[Common Artifact:Carbamyl on K]DTC[Common Fixed:Carbamidomethyl on C]FSTEGPNLVTR|[Common Artifact:Carbamyl on X]AADKDTC[Common Fixed:Carbamidomethyl on C]FSTEGPNLVTR`, `AAVAASGLNTVLEGD[Metal:Magnesium on D]GQFTLLAPTNEAFEK|AAVAASGLNTVLE[Metal:Magnesium on E]GDGQFTLLAPTNEAFEK`, `AR[Common Artifact:Carbamyl on R]PNC[Common Fixed:Carbamidomethyl on C]GGNLLGVR|[Common Artifact:Carbamyl on X]ARPNC[Common Fixed:Carbamidomethyl on C]GGNLLGVR`."
   },
   {
    "code": "sdrf_skeleton",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "The deposited SDRF carries no biological annotation: organism part, cell type, disease and individual are all absent. Sample-level questions cannot be answered for this dataset until it is curated."
   },
   {
    "code": "unplaced_ptm_sites",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "Some modifications on peptides shared between proteins were not written to ptm_sites for one or more of those proteins, because the peptide could not be located in that protein's sequence and the producer's residue spans cannot be paired with its accessions. Of the (PSM, protein) pairs affected: 401 named a protein that does not contain the stored peptide -- typically a PSM ambiguous between peptide sequences (level 4 or 5), where this protein carries a different candidate than the first, which is the one stored. Sites on the other proteins of the same PSMs are written. Counts are in bundle.json under protein_databases."
   },
   {
    "code": "occupancy_decoy_groups",
    "severity": "info",
    "message": "5 occupancy entries on decoy protein groups were not stored: MetaMorpheus computes them, and they are FDR machinery, not biology."
   },
   {
    "code": "run_counts_missing",
    "severity": "info",
    "message": "No per-run `metrics` row from results.txt for `psms_1pct` (12 of 12 runs), `peptides` (12 of 12 runs), `protein_groups` (12 of 12 runs), `precursors` (12 of 12 runs), `ms2_scans` (12 of 12 runs). These counts were not written, which is not a count of zero. The search task sets `WriteIndividualFiles = false`, and MetaMorpheus writes results.txt's per-file PSM, peptide and protein-group lines only when it is true (before 1.1.14, MetaMorpheus #2955, its per-file precursor and MS2 lines too). Each run's MS2 spectra are also counted by the QC report, in `runs.ms2_spectra` and `metrics` (`name = 'ms2'`, `source = 'qc_report.json'`), for 12 of the 12 runs. PXReprise's QC payload counts each run's share of the whole search's 1% set instead, a different number (the FDR is the whole search's, not recomputed on each file), under names of its own (`source = 'qc_payload.json'`): `psms_1pct_whole_search` for 12 of the 12 runs, `peptides_1pct_whole_search` for 12 of the 12 runs, `protein_groups_1pct_whole_search` for 12 of the 12 runs."
   }
  ],
